binomialIsPrimary -- test for primary binomial ideals
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        binomialIsPrime I
  * Inputs:
      * I, a binomial ideal
  * Outputs:
      * true or false, depending on whether I is a primary binomial ideal

Description
===========

A binomial ideal is prime only if it is cellular. If the cellular variables are
known, the function *note cellularBinomialIsPrimary: cellularBinomialIsPrimary,
should be used.
+------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]      |
|                        |
|o1 = R                  |
|                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing     |
+------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x-y,z^3) |
|                        |
|                    3   |
|o2 = ideal (x - y, z )  |
|                        |
|o2 : Ideal of R         |
+------------------------+
|i3 : binomialIsPrimary I|
|                        |
|o3 = true               |
+------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note cellularBinomialIsPrimary: cellularBinomialIsPrimary, -- test for
    primaryness of a binomial ideal
  * *note CellVariables: CellVariables, -- cellular variables

