binomialRadical -- Radical of a binomial ideal
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        binomialRadical I
  * Inputs:
      * I, a binomial ideal
  * Outputs:
      * the radical of I

Description
===========

If the input is a cellular binomial ideal then a very fast algorithm is used.
If one knows this and also the cellular variables then *note
cellularBinomialRadical: cellularBinomialRadical, should be used.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]                   |
|                                   |
|o1 = R                             |
|                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal (y^2, x*y-y, x^2-1) |
|                                   |
|             2            2        |
|o2 = ideal (y , x*y - y, x  - 1)   |
|                                   |
|o2 : Ideal of R                    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : binomialRadical I             |
|                                   |
|             2            2        |
|o3 = ideal (y , x*y - y, x  - 1, y)|
|                                   |
|o3 : Ideal of R                    |
+-----------------------------------+

