extractInclusionMinimalIdeals -- Extract inclusion minimal ideals from a list of ideals
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        extractInclusionMinimalIdeals L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a list of ideals
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Verbose: binomialPrimaryDecomposition_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_
        pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value false, generate informative output
  * Outputs:
      * the list with some redundant ideals removed

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b]                                         |
|                                                         |
|o1 = R                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = {ideal(a^4),ideal(a^3),ideal(a^5),ideal(b^2*a) }|
|                                                         |
|             4         3         5           2           |
|o2 = {ideal a , ideal a , ideal a , ideal(a*b )}         |
|                                                         |
|o2 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : extractInclusionMinimalIdeals L                     |
|                                                         |
|             5           2                               |
|o3 = {ideal a , ideal(a*b )}                             |
|                                                         |
|o3 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
This function is mostly for internal purposes.

Caveat
======

The resulting list may be not irredundant, because I_1 \subset I_2 \cap I_3 is
not checked.

