latticeBasisIdeal -- construct the ideal whose generators correspond to generators of an integer lattice
********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        latticeBasisIdeal (R,L)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a ring
      * L, an integer matrix whose columns span the lattice.
  * Outputs:
      * The unital lattice basis ideal in R, defined by L

Description
===========

This function is only a very simple wrapper around *note makeBinomial:
makeBinomial,
+------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                  |
|                                    |
|o1 = R                              |
|                                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                 |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = matrix {{1,1},{-3,0},{0,1}}|
|                                    |
|o2 = | 1  1 |                       |
|     | -3 0 |                       |
|     | 0  1 |                       |
|                                    |
|              3       2             |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ              |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : latticeBasisIdeal (R, L)       |
|                                    |
|               3                    |
|o3 = ideal (- y  + x, x*z - 1)      |
|                                    |
|o3 : Ideal of R                     |
