PartialCharacter -- the class of all partial characters
*******************************************************

Description
===========

In *note Binomials: Top, the partial character of a cellular binomial ideal is
represented as an object of class *note PartialCharacter: PartialCharacter,.
It contains the following three data:
  * J -- the cellular variables
  * L -- a matrix whose columns are generators for the lattice
  * c -- the list of values the character takes on the generators

Methods that use an object of class PartialCharacter:
=====================================================

  * "idealFromCharacter(Ring,PartialCharacter)" -- see *note
    idealFromCharacter: idealFromCharacter, -- Generate a lattice ideal from a
    character.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note PartialCharacter: PartialCharacter, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

