File: Binomials.info, Node: partialCharacter, Next: randomBinomialIdeal, Prev: PartialCharacter, Up: Top

partialCharacter -- Computing the partial character of a cellular binomial ideal
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        partialCharacter I
  * Inputs:
      * I, a cellular binomial ideal
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CellVariables: CellVariables, => ..., default value null,
        cellular variables
  * Outputs:
      * the *note PartialCharacter: PartialCharacter,

Description
===========

If the cell variables are known, they can be given via the option *note
CellVariables: CellVariables, otherwise they are computed.
+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]                                |
|                                                |
|o1 = R                                          |
|                                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                             |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^3-1,y-x)                       |
|                                                |
|             3                                  |
|o2 = ideal (x  - 1, - x + y)                    |
|                                                |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : cv = isCellular (I,ReturnCellVars=>true)   |
|                                                |
|o3 = {x, y}                                     |
|                                                |
|o3 : List                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : pc = partialCharacter (I,CellVariables=>cv)|
|                                                |
|o4 = PartialCharacter{"c" => {1, 1}  }          |
|                      "J" => {x, y}             |
|                      "L" => | 1  0 |           |
|                             | -1 3 |           |
|                                                |
|o4 : PartialCharacter                           |
+------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

If the input is not cellular the behaviour is undefined. Cellularity is not
checked.

Ways to use partialCharacter:
=============================

  * "partialCharacter(Ideal)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note partialCharacter: partialCharacter, is a *note method function
with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

